<title>PAKISTAN: Pakistani cotton rates close steady.</title>
<headline>Pakistani cotton rates close steady.</headline>
<dateline>KARACHI, Pakistan 1996-12-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Pakistani cotton rates closed steady on Wednesday amid continued buying of good quality cotton by spinners, brokers said.</p>
<p>Exporters stayed out of the market due to high domestic prices, broker Nasim Usman said.</p>
<p>In the kerb market, the rate for MNH-93 variety was quoted around 2,620 rupees per maund (37.32 kg), while NIAB-78 was quoted above 2,540 rupees per maund, he said.  </p>
<p>Wednesday's Karachi Cotton Association official spot rates in rupees per maund including 10 percent sales tax:</p>
<p>				     Wednesday	  December 3</p>
<p>    NIAB-78			2,405		2,405</p>
<p>    K-68			   2,597.50	   2,597.50</p>
<p>    MNH-93			 2,618.50	   2,618.50</p>
<p>($1 = 40.22 rupees) -- Ibrahim Khan 9221-5685192</p>
</text>
